Paris is located in northern central France, in a north-bending arc of the river Seine, whose crest includes two islands, the Île Saint-Louis and the larger Île de la Cité, which form the oldest part of Paris. The river's mouth on the English Channel (La Manche) is about 233 mi (375 km) downstream from Paris. Paris is spread widely on both banks of the river. Overall, Paris is relatively flat, and the lowest point is 35 m (115 ft) above sea level. Paris has several prominent hills, the highest of which is Montmartre at 130 m (427 ft). ([Geography](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris#Geography))

Topics: [Geography of Paris](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geography_of_Paris) — overview of the geography of Paris

